WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.310
We only have to do one more thing to win...

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.440
Totally destroy all 
the relationships in Group K.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.440
<b>Totally destroy them</b>

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.440
<b>Totally destroy them</b>

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.010
<b>Episode 10: The Third Game Is Over!</b>

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.240
<b>Episode 10: The Third Game Is Over!</b>

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.610
Destroy Group K's relationships...

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.280
But how?

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.200
Remember what I asked Manabu 
when we got our third teammate?

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.830
If it was a girl or not?

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.960
Yeah. What I'm trying to set right now

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.890
is a honey trap.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.470
U-Um, thank you very much.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.380
I owe you my life.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.470
M-Me?

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.180
W-Wait a sec.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.280
Between the two of us, shouldn't it be him?

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.280
Ah, well, I just did what 
any guy would have done!

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>Glare</b>

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.490
<b>Glare</b>

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:57.410
<b></b>Hmph!

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.500
I hate this guy!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.080
I caught him peeping at me when I was naked!

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.190
Th-That's not true! It was an accident!

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.170
And you weren't naked, you had underwear on!

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.620
You saw her in her underwear?

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.050
Yeah! No! Well, I did see her 
underwear, but only for a second!

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.380
I don't even remember it!

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.670
Really? You really don't remember it at all?

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.460
I'm so sorry! I totally remember!

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.930
It's branded in my memory!

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.060
I lied. I'm just kidding.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.020
I truly owe you my life, too.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.360
Thank you very much for saving me.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.210
Ah—

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.040
Anyway, what was Katagiri Yuichi thinking?

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.670
What would have happened to you 
if Hyakutaro wasn't there to catch you?

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.000
<i>She must have been terrified.</i>

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.780
I'll never forgive that asshole.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.550
He's the worst kind of trash!

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.220
Please stop saying bad things about him!

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.640
W-Why are you sticking up
 for a guy like that?

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:07.100
I'm sorry, but...

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.480
If he finds out that I was talking 
to the other team like this, I...

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.490
Anyway, Yuichi got away from us, 
so let's go back to the food station.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.950
Y-Yeah.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.450
Ow!

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.290
Are you hurt?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.500
N-No, it's nothing.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.490
Here.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.880
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:40.250
There are times when I really admire 
your assertive personality, Hyakutaro.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.880
Shut up. My granny always 
told me to be nice to girls.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.850
You really are a kind person, 
aren't you, Hyakutaro-kun?

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.600
Why...

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.360
Why did I have to end up in Group C?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.160
I see. So that's what happened.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:08.770
If Group C succeeded in procuring food, 
we might be in for a really long fight.

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.900
Katagiri Yuichi!

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.210
Oh, I'm totally up for a long fight.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.590
You think you can just waltz 
back in here, asshole?

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:22.760
Hey, Maria. What are you doing?
 Get over here.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.390
Let's start fresh! I wanna 
take my time and enjoy this.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.560
Hey. Get away from the girl.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:34.770
Why?

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.650
Did you forget what you did?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.650
Look at her! She's been 
shaking the whole time!

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.570
Oh, I doubt that.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:46.780
Right, Maria? We're on the same team, right?!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.790
Y-Yes.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.790
You'd better cut that shit out.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:57.170
Huh? Why hold back with
 something that belongs to me?

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.590
You piece of...

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.680
Let's go!

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.180
Stop! This is exactly what 
he wants you to do!

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.010
Shit.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.210
Damn it, Maria! Don't get in my way!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.290
Manabu-kun, he's being violent!

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:17.180
This is clearly in-game violence, isn't it?

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.150
Yeah, it sure is.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:23.610
But that's violence against a teammate.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.740
What's prohibited is violent acts 
against the <i>other</i> team.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Can't Do</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Violence</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Moving the Hider</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Can Do</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Contact</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Food</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Surrender (Give Up)</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
<b><b>Change Sides (Switch)</b></b>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.450
<b>Third Game Rule</b>

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.450
<b><b>Can't Do</b></b>

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.450
<b><b>Violence</b></b>

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.450
<b>It is forbidden to use violence against another group
 and force them to give up the hider's location.</b>

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.940
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:36.040
I can do whatever I want to this chick 
and it won't break any rules.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.020
Ouch!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.340
Please... Please, stop!

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.090
Is this Katagiri Yuichi's true personality?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.730
What color is your blood?

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:47.070
Why did I have to end up in Group C?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:49.890
Oh, that's it!

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.180
Why don't you switch to our team?

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.130
No, wait a minute.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.600
Something's off, here. 
It all seems too perfect.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.690
<i>Huh, I guess this guy's 
experience with women</i>

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:03.260
<i>has made him really cautious around them.</i>

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.710
Can't you see they might be playing us?

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.250
Playing us how?

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.410
You can't mean she's been 
acting the whole time.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.120
I hate to say it, but that's 
exactly what I mean.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.720
That was all an act?

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.290
Y'know, not everyone in 
the world is like you,

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.380
screwin' off,

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.380
puttin' on a front,

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:24.300
and livin' the easy life, asshole.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.680
<i>What an idiot.</i>

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.300
<i>Those are land mines for a guy like him.</i>

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.430
You...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:30.890
What?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:34.180
You think I'm screwing off 
for the fun of it?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.330
A virgin like you wouldn't 
understand anything, anyway.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.860
All women are capable of putting on 
an act to get what they want.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:44.000
T-That's so mean!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:45.930
Chisato!

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:49.490
What, you wanna show off 
in front of the girl?

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:53.330
Violence against teammates 
is okay, you know?

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.670
Okay, stop right there, please.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.270
We decided no fighting during 
the Tomodachi Game, remember?

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:05.840
Also, the captain has
the final say on everything.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.470
Is it time for Captain-sama to 
make an appearance again?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.660
Yes, it is.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.850
That's how we've been able to 
clear the Tomodachi Game so far.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.540
You can't make up your own 
mind to protect one girl?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.560
That's pathetic, son.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.440
Wait a second, Kei.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.530
I'll call the captain and convince him myself.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.160
Very well.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.160
Why don't we both go talk to 
the captain together, then?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.850
It'll be easier to explain 
your feelings directly.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.020
Okay.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.120
Banri-senpai,

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:42.190
if you don't mind, please call us 
right away if they give any indication

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.790
that they might try to follow us.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.720
Mizuse-san, just hang 
in there a little longer.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.680
<i>Everything's going really smoothly.</i>

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:02.840
<i>Group K's captain, who's the pillar of the team, 
has been absent during the third game.</i>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
<b>Kadokura Juzo</b>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
-The team leader
-Psychological pillar
-Considerate of his friends
-Self-sacrificing 
-Strong sense of responsibility

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
<b>Onigawara Hyakutaro</b>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
-Impulsive 
-Strong sense of duty 
-Acts tough but weak for women 
-Kindest of the bunch 
-An idiot

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
<b>Shinomiya Kei</b>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
-The youngest
-Small and weaker than the rest
-Cocky
-In charge of contacting Captain
-Debt holder?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
<b>Niwa Banri</b>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
-Silent type
-Bland
-Barely noticeable
-Steady-handed
-Manga otaku?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
<b>Hashiratani Chisato</b>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:09.780
-Calm and composed
-Prudent
-Seems flirty but distrusts women
-Dilettante 
-Probably really gloomy

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:06.880
<i>Since he isn't here to smooth 
over little conflicts in the group,</i>

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:09.780
<b></b>Opposite personality, so really annoying

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:09.780
<b></b>Opposite personality, so really annoying

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:09.780
<i>the connection between Hyakutaro 
and Chisato has become really fragile.</i>

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:13.780
<i>Most likely, the captain will agree 
to let Maria switch over.</i>

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.870
<i>But, as we planned, 
Maria will reject that idea.</i>

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.300
<i>Obviously, Hyakutaro will try to press her,</i>

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.000
<i>and she'll tell him that 
I'm holding something over her.</i>

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.710
<i>I came up with something 
really shocking for that.</i>

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.620
<i>Then Hyakutaro will fly 
into a rage and punch me.</i>

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.840
<i>That would be our easiest way to win.</i>

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.220
<i>His teammates might hold him back,</i>

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:38.220
<i>but friction in the group will increase 
and their relationships will crack.</i>

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.310
<i>Ultimately, I'll maneuver 
Hyakutaro toward one decision.</i>

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:47.070
Hyakutaro-kun, I can't 
take this alone anymore.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.320
<i>And that will be for him to switch sides.</i>

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:54.160
<i>If we can pull that off, 
we'll definitely win.</i>

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.410
<i>Once he's on our side, 
I have any number of ways</i>

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.700
<i>to force him to spill 
the captain's location.</i>

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.210
<b>Several Hours Later...</b>

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.570
We're back.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.190
So, what did Captain say?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:11.720
It's no good. He said 
he won't let you switch.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.200
Well that settles it, then.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.390
But Captain said one more thing:

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:22.600
"If you still want to protect her, 
there is one other way," he said.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.230
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.730
Wait a second! What are you thinking?!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.900
Shut up! I've made up my mind!

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:30.940
Just calm down!

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.610
Let go of me!

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.920
Don't do it, Hyakutaro!

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:37.280
I know you don't give a damn 
about how I feel!

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.530
Manabu!

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.530
Huh?

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.500
I'm switchin' to Group C!

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.500
Of course I approve!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:50.710
Then from this moment forward, 
Onigawara Hyakutaro is a member of Group C!

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.150
Sorry, guys.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:56.640
But even though I'm Group C now, 
I don't plan on working with 'em.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.600
I'm prepared to get more debt 
when you guys win.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.850
Keep playing. I won't hold you back.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:07.480
Welcome to Group C! 
I'm happy to have you, Hyakutaro-kun.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.610
Yeah.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:13.360
Now I can pop you one without holding back!

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:17.980
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:19.780
I knew you'd take a swing at me.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.240
Your moves are so easy to read, kid.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.870
Sorry, but I'm not going to let you 
be violent in either group.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.210
I hope you don't mind being tied up.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.240
Well then, maybe now's a good time to go 
and talk tactics with your Captain-sama!

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.420
Don't worry. We won't try to follow you.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.300
What's going on, Yuichi?

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.450
<i>I was able to get one Group K 
member to switch to our group.</i>

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.730
I-It hasn't even been one day yet!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.890
<i>Everything fell into place.</i>

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.680
<i>Now I just need to get 
the hiding place out of him.</i>

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:51.980
<i>Then we win.</i>

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.400
All right, then.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.950
<i>Don't get carried away, Yuichi.</i>

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:56.920
Of course.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.780
If I can help it, I don't 
want to get rough, either.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.160
I'll contact you later.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.310
<i>Okay.</i>

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.190
I really let you down.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.960
I wanted to help, but ended up like this.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.840
It's okay! It made me really happy.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:17.210
But at this rate, I'm sure he'll 
do horrible things to you

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:18.930
to make you tell us where
 the captain's hiding place—

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.800
Not a problem! I know 
I'm tough enough to take it.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:25.560
You can't! He'll do anything 
he possibly can to win.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.720
H-He's even murdered people before.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:30.350
M-Murder?!

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:33.230
I couldn't stand to watch 
something like that!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.570
<b></b>Call in progress

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.570
<b></b>Katagiri Yuichi (Group C)

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.760
Then it'd be better if I tell him now, 
so you don't have to suffer.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.060
<i>We've won.</i>

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.070
<i>But, I can't do it.</i>

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:44.210
<i>Because actually, I...</i>

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.120
<i>don't know where the captain 
is in the first place.</i>

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.750
<i>W-What did he say? What does this mean?!</i>

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.130
Everything fell into place.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.780
<i>I-I can't possibly have...</i>

00:10:56.780 --> 00:11:01.260
About time! It looks like our genius 
is finally making his play.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.260
Are you sure that was the best move?

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.440
Hyakutaro insisted on switching, 
just like you suggested.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:12.270
It's fine, it's fine. 
It's all part of my plan.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.650
But more importantly...

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:17.360
I told you to speak to me 
politely when we're alone,

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.040
you blockhead.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.330
So, this is your monster?

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.530
Just look at  this pathetic little thing.

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:25.680
Listen up!

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.410
A true genius is someone who controls

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:26.280
<b></b>Gloat

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.040
<b></b>Gloat

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:27.790
<b></b>Gloat

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:31.230
and manipulates everything 
from the shadows. Got it?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:28.540
<b></b>Gloat

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:29.290
<b></b>Gloat

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.040
<b></b>Gloat

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:32.040
Lame.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:31.790
<b>Lame</b>

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.050
Hey, Hyakutaro!

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.140
Why didn't you visit the Captain?

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.590
You said you were going to 
talk to him directly!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:42.930
Well, because on the way there, 
Kei said he got a call telling us

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.540
to come back because you guys 
were up to something.

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:49.730
"We don't have a choice. 
We'll have to call him."

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:51.300
That's what Kei said.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.230
<b></b>Incoming call

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.230
<b></b>Katagiri Yuichi (Group C)

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.070
Hello, this is Shinomiya Kei.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.650
It was you all along. 
The true leader of Group K.

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.320
Oh, did you finally figure it out?

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:10.540
Honestly, I underestimated you guys. 
So I didn't even notice...

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:15.670
that you were controlling Group K's
 movements at every step.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.970
But at least I realized 
before things got worse.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:21.110
I won't make another mistake!

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:23.300
<i>Oh, so scary.</i>

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:27.910
Too bad, though. We've already 
secured our victory for this game,

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:32.230
right when you let that time bomb 
Hyakutaro join your team.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.850
Hyakutaro's a bomb?

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.600
<i>You should be bright enough to understand.</i>

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:37.900
<i>You're no match for me,</i>

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.480
but the gears in your head do seem 
to be turning just a little.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.530
W-What's wrong?

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:44.790
They got us.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:49.250
At this rate, we'll definitely lose.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.530
<b></b>Definitely lose...

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.960
You seem very pleased, Prince.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.630
Do I?

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.080
Well, I guess I am.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.760
Thanks to Katagiri Yuichi, I wasn't
 bored at all for the last few days.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:05.930
In that sense, I should thank you 
for giving me this chance.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.640
It's all over now, though.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:12.040
All that's left is finishing 
off the checked king.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.850
Is our victory truly assured?

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:19.690
Well, yeah. But a blockhead like 
you wouldn't see it, would you?

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.540
There are two main points.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:25.030
Hyakutaro switched sides, but 
had no intention of betraying us.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.450
And in this game, if the other 
team uses violence against you,

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.910
the game ends immediately.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:33.450
I see. So that's why 
Hyakutaro's a time bomb.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:38.810
If you get it, keep giving everyone 
orders in your oh-so-dignified way.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.000
I'm going to take care of something else.

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:42.880
Something else?

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:45.010
Well, since I have the chance,

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:48.590
I thought I'd find the enemy hider 
and go for a clean win.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:52.010
Shinomiya Kei. What's his story?

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.100
There's no story. 
He's a genius, plain and simple.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.240
His family and upbringing 
are extremely normal.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:59.980
<b>Rank                 Score                     Name</b>

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:59.980
<b></b>Shinomiya Kei

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:59.980
<b></b>Fujii Satoshi

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:59.980
<b></b>Watanabe Katsu {cut off}

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.980
He's simply a genius who can 
do anything he puts his mind to.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.650
His one and only flaw

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:04.920
is that he's so good at everything, 
he gets bored very quickly.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:08.280
In fact, I think he joined the game just 
to kill time because he was bored.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:11.160
Playing the Tomodachi Game to kill time...

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.160
But even then, he immediately 
found a strategy—

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:20.530
to manipulate the very well-trusted 
Kadokura Juzo from the shadows,

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.550
and control Group K through him.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:27.170
Why is Kadokura Juzo obeying his orders?

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:30.300
Who knows? Maybe Shinomiya found 
his weak point or something.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.560
Weak point, huh?

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:38.730
Either way, the game is over. 
The genius has already announced his victory.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.650
This is bad. Really bad.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:43.860
This is the worst situation 
I could have imagined.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.360
<i>Huh? What? Is he serious right now?</i>

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:49.470
Um, why is it so bad?

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:50.620
Because of violence.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.280
Huh?

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:57.750
If Hyakutaro, who's now in Group C, attacks 
someone in Group K, we'll lose immediately.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.290
<b>Pow!</b>

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:02.250
So I tied him up, but I did that 
expecting to win right away.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:06.060
Since that isn't happening now, 
Hyakutaro is a time bomb.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:09.830
We have to watch him 24/7 
to make sure he doesn't blow up.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:15.350
That means we can't move one step from here.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:18.230
Wait a minute...

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:20.890
If we can hide Hyakutaro 
somewhere before they come...

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.010
Not a chance. You're too late.

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:26.570
You are already dead.

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:29.180
Banri-san! Chisato!

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:34.010
Well, then, ready for another endurance test?

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.490
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.460
Hey! Where are you going?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:48.090
That's not a question you should ask a girl.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.140
Oh, sorry.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.770
Ah, I'm getting so sick of this.

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:01.390
Is that right, Mizuse Maria-san?

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:04.020
Huh? Oh, no, that was just...

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.400
I'm sorry for startling you.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.980
Actually, I was waiting to catch you alone.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:09.940
Huh?

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:12.360
This is awkward, so let me cut
 right to the chase.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:16.910
You're from the management, right?

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.850
H-How?

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:20.370
<i>My cover's blown!</i>

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.130
It feels stupid explaining it like this,

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:25.400
but for three days before 
the game, our food rations

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:27.290
were based on how many 
group members we had, right?

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.270
Since Group C had just two people,

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:32.050
They were only given water, 
the poor things.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:36.510
But even though you showed up alone, 
you didn't appear hungry at all.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.920
Now, doesn't that seem strange?

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:41.790
Any way you look at it, 
you're not an ordinary player.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:45.000
So it made sense to assume you 
were on the management side.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:45.940
Achoo!

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:46.770
Hmm?

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:50.800
I mean, I could ask you to tell me 
about your original team instead,

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.160
but what do you think?

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.700
Why bother?

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:58.490
What now? What do you want from me?

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.450
I'll just cut right to the chase again.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:05.580
I'd like you to betray Katagiri Yuichi.

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:09.960
That... That's just a little...

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:14.220
You can do that, can't you? Right now, 
Group K is going to win, without a doubt.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.970
If you wanted to keep 
acting like a normal player,

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.680
wouldn't it actually seem weird 
 <i>not</i> to betray him?

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:24.130
But y'know, since I <i>did</i> try 
to play cute and innocent,

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.620
I wonder if betraying him now 
would seem unlike me.

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:28.730
Ah, so the issue is character.

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:33.650
But you seem like the kind of person 
to choose fun over reason and logic.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:36.100
<i>Huh, he's really figured me out.</i>

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:38.110
To put it simply,

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:41.080
you'll have more fun with me.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.450
If you betray him for me, 
you'll get to enjoy

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:47.730
watching that overconfident, 
sadistic Katagiri Yuichi

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:51.090
crumble into a pathetic, teary-eyed failure.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:55.850
T-That sounds like...

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:03.390
It would be super fun!

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:10.920
Yes?

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:14.400
<i>It's Maria. Is anyone else nearby?</i>

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:19.610
No. I'm being watched, 
but they aren't close enough to hear.

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:24.450
Could you please tell me where 
Mikasa Tenji's hiding spot is?

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:25.460
What?

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:28.830
<i>Luckily, I'm alone right now,</i>

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.150
<i>so I think it would be a good idea</i>

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:33.040
<i>to transport additional 
food supplies while I can.</i>

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:36.920
I think the only thing we can do 
now is buy time, anyway.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:42.760
<i>If we have more time, I'm sure you'll be 
able to find a way to turn things around.</i>

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:45.890
Fine. I'll tell you.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.530
Hey! Why are you with them?

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.950
Wait, you didn't...

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.530
Did you betray us?

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:12.080
G... G... God...

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:17.550
God damn it!

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.050
It appears that he did give her 
the hider's true location.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.280
There's nothing he can do 
now even if we leave him,

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.560
so why don't we all start
 searching before it gets dark?

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:29.680
This is hell.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.830
It can't get any worse than this!

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.320
<i>Hello, Mikasa Tenji-senpai.</i>

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.030
It's nice speaking to you again.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.700
This is Shinomiya Kei from Group K.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:50.940
<i>But wow, that Katagiri Yuichi 
sure is the lowest of the low.</i>

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:51.920
What are you saying?

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:56.290
He's totally happy to let you die 
if it gets him the win.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:20:00.170
By my estimation, he's planning 
something really evil right now.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:03.460
<i>You should cut ties with that 
inhuman brute as soon as you can.</i>

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.930
What makes you think you know anything?

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.600
Huh? What was that? 
I couldn't really hear you.

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:13.160
If you've got something to say to me, 
you'd better speak up, dude.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.790
Quit shooting your mouth off! 
You don't know a damn thing!

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.980
I'm betting on Yuichi!

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.490
<i>Wow, you startled me.</i>

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:26.440
<i>But I heard you loud 
and clear, thanks to that.</i>

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:30.190
Found you!

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:38.180
And that concludes the third game!

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.720
<i>Sergeant Manabu here.</i>

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.110
<i>The game has ended.</i>

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:46.590
<i>All players, including hiders, 
immediately gather at the food station.</i>

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:49.010
All right! I'm on my way!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:52.110
<i>He lost? Yuichi lost?</i>

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:54.390
Don't look so upset.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.600
You all did your very best.

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:59.610
You just got the wrong opponents this time.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:03.110
I am a genius, after all.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:09.510
God damn it!

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:13.580
Now, everyone's back together again.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.580
Let's announce the results pronto!

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:21.910
The winner of the third game, 
Friendly Hide-and-Seek, is...

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:27.760
Katagiri Yuichi... he's a devil!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:32.770
Yes, he probably brings misery 
to everyone he touches.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.260
<b>YOU COCKROACH</b>

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.260
<b></b>family of crooks

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.260
<b>Die!</b>

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.260
<b>Don't ever come back
 to this school!!</b>

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b>FILTHY THIEF!</b>

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b>DIE CRIMINAL</b>

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b></b>die

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b>Give it back,
 asshole</b>

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b></b>We'll find you

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b>you piece of shit</b>

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b>GIVE THE MONEY BACK THIEF</b>

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.260
<b></b>you suck

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:38.820
Ultimately, the essence of the 
Tomodachi Game may be that it asks you,

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:41.900
"How many of your friends' sins 
are you willing to forgive?"

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:46.950
<b>NEXT: Do You Really Have Nothing You Care About?</b>
